// ServUO: Spawns/Eodon.xml, the XmlSpawner file ServUO's [DecorateTOL loads with "[XmlLoad Spawns/Eodon.xml"
// (Services/Expansions/TimeOfLegends.cs:79, cc-P198), carried as data in file order, one row per <Points> element
// kept (generated by gen_eodon_spawns.py, notes). The P196 BlackthornSpawns shape.
//
// XmlSpawner -> ModernUO Spawner, field by field (every value below is the XML's):
//   <Name>                     Name, ServUO's ("Eodon_Wildlife #9", "Vof1_Silverback1", ...).
//   <Map>                      Ter Mur on every kept row (the two Trammel rows are Hawkwind's quest, dropped).
//   <CentreX/Y/Z>              Location.
//   <X> <Y> <Width> <Height>   SpawnBounds, at full Z range like ModernUO's own legacy import (BaseSpawner.cs:323-341),
//                              except the Barako village rows, whose entries carry XmlSpawner's "/Z/100" (spawn, then
//                              set Z to 100: the clifftop the climbing vines reach). Pinned's spawner picks z inside
//                              its bounds (BaseSpawner.GetSpawnPosition, :457-468), so those rows get bounds from z 100
//                              to 110 instead, which puts them on the same clifftop.
//   <Range>                    WalkingRange.   <IsHomeRangeRelative> SpawnLocationIsHome (true on every row).
//   <MaxCount>                 Count, capped at the sum of the kept entries (the four desert rows: below).
//   <MinDelay>/<MaxDelay>      minutes on every row (DelayInSec False), carried as seconds: 1-2 minutes, 60-120 s.
//   <Objects2> type:MX=n       one entry per type, maxCount n and probability n: XmlSpawner draws among the entries
//                              below their limit weighted by MaxCount (XmlSpawner2.cs:8377-8408), pinned weighted by
//                              probability (BaseSpawner.cs:867-893), so the same weights give ServUO's mix (cc-P458;
//                              a flat 100 made a white tiger 1 in 8 on Wildlife #4, not 1 in 25). Type names
//                              case-corrected. A
//                              "TribeWarrior,Kurak" entry's argument is the tribe, passed as the entry's Parameters
//                              (BaseSpawner.cs:1024-1047 parses it into the [Constructible] TribeWarrior(EodonTribe)).
//   Everything else            XmlSpawner defaults on every row (checked: no proximity, time of day, sequence, group,
//                              despawn or trigger anywhere in the file).
//
// Dropped, 19 rows and part of 4 (in the notes, with the reason for each):
//   - Myrmidex (out of scope by name): MyrmidexLarvae/Drone/Warrior on the four Eodon_Desert rows. Their spiders and
//     scorpions stay, so each of those rows asks for fewer than ServUO's MaxCount.
//   - The Valley of One quest line (declined in CC3 with its quest framework): the five tribal high chiefs, Sir
//     Geoffery, the tiger cub enclosures, the dragon turtle nests, the T-Rex, the great ape and the volcano
//     elementals, all defined in Quests/Eodon/Valley of One Quest/.
//   - Hawkwind (Quests/Eodon/Hawkwind, a quest NPC): the Eodon row and the two Trammel rows (one an xmlquestnpc).
//   - Three "WanderingShaman" entries with MX=0 on the swamp rows: XmlSpawner never spawns them; no entry here.
//
// Every kept type exists: stock pinned (LavaSerpent, LavaSnake, FireElemental, LavaLizard, TropicalBird,
// VampireBat, Corpser, AirElemental, Gorilla, ForestOstard, GiantBlackWidow, Panther, Wisp, SandVortex, Alligator,
// BullFrog, GiantToad, AcidElemental) or ported (the seven dinosaurs and SilverbackGorilla, CC3 and this task;
// WildTiger and its two children, cc-P129; the tribesmen, DesertScorpion and WanderingShaman, this task).

